% ============================================================================
% vitamin-deficiency-symptom — for five of the seven vitamins already tabled
% in vitamins.adj, the SYMPTOM described in the same already-quoted NIH span
% that names the deficiency disease (adj-facts-stdlib, BIOLOGY).
% ============================================================================
% A sibling to the already-shipped `vitamins.adj`
% (`deficiency_disease(vitamin, disease)`, the classic deficiency DISEASE
% each vitamin's lack causes — vitamin_c → scurvy, vitamin_d → rickets,
% etc.). That table's own header already quotes, verbatim, the NIH ODS
% sentence that states each disease, and for five of the seven vitamins the
% SAME sentence also states the disease's defining SYMPTOM — a fact the
% disease-name-only schema had no room for:
%
%   vitamin_a → inability_to_see_in_low_light
%     "Xerophthalmia is the inability to see in low light, and it can lead
%      to blindness if it isn't treated."
%
%   vitamin_d → soft_weak_deformed_painful_bones
%     "vitamin D deficiency causes rickets, a disease in which the bones
%      become soft, weak, deformed, and painful."
%
%   vitamin_b1 → tingling_and_numbness_in_feet_and_hands
%     "beriberi with the added symptoms of tingling and numbness in the
%      feet and hands, loss of muscle, and poor reflexes."
%
%   vitamin_b9 → weakness_and_fatigue
%     "megaloblastic anemia, a blood disorder that causes weakness,
%      fatigue, trouble concentrating, irritability, headache, heart
%      palpitations, and shortness of breath."
%
%   vitamin_b12 → tired_and_weak
%     "megaloblastic anemia, a blood condition that makes people tired and
%      weak."
%
% Recall is a binding query:
%
%     ? vitamin_deficiency_symptom(vitamin_d, $Symptom)   % soft_weak_deformed_painful_bones
%
% This is a native `table` (ADJ-TABLES RS-5, an ordinary two-column EXACT
% lookup): each `row` lowers to a ground relation
% `vitamin_deficiency_symptom(vitamin, symptom)` carrying the citation, so
% the lookup above is the ordinary SLD binding query — the engine returns
% the symptom WITH its source, on the CPU, with zero model calls. Two of
% the parent table's seven vitamins have NO symptom clause in their already-
% quoted span — `vitamin_c`'s cited sentence only states the mg threshold
% and the disease name ("...can get scurvy"), and `vitamin_b3`'s cited
% sentence only names the disease ("...leads to a disease called
% pellagra") — so this sibling is HONESTLY NARROWER than its parent: it
% grounds exactly the five vitamins whose cited span states a symptom, and
% abstains on `vitamin_c`, `vitamin_b3`, or any other word, rather than
% inventing a symptom neither cited sentence contains. The query also runs
% BACKWARD — bind a symptom and recall which vitamin's deficiency causes
% it:
%
%     ? vitamin_deficiency_symptom($V, tired_and_weak)
%       % vitamin_b12
%
% Provenance: reproduces, byte-for-byte, five of the seven NIH Office of
% Dietary Supplements spans already quoted inside `vitamins.adj`'s own
% header — no new WebFetch, only a different schema decoding the symptom
% half of each already-verified quote. `trust authoritative` — the same
% tier `vitamins.adj` already carries (NIH ODS, a primary U.S. government
% consumer fact sheet).
% (See ../README.md; feedback_nothing_human_authored,
% feedback_adj_only_shipped_artifacts.)
% ============================================================================

table vitamin_deficiency_symptom {
    columns vitamin, symptom

    row (vitamin_a, inability_to_see_in_low_light)              % NIH: "Xerophthalmia is the inability to see in low light, and it can lead to blindness if it isn't treated."
    row (vitamin_d, soft_weak_deformed_painful_bones)            % NIH: "vitamin D deficiency causes rickets, a disease in which the bones become soft, weak, deformed, and painful."
    row (vitamin_b1, tingling_and_numbness_in_feet_and_hands)    % NIH: "beriberi with the added symptoms of tingling and numbness in the feet and hands, loss of muscle, and poor reflexes."
    row (vitamin_b9, weakness_and_fatigue)                       % NIH: "megaloblastic anemia, a blood disorder that causes weakness, fatigue, trouble concentrating, irritability, headache, heart palpitations, and shortness of breath."
    row (vitamin_b12, tired_and_weak)                            % NIH: "megaloblastic anemia, a blood condition that makes people tired and weak."

    source "Xerophthalmia is the inability to see in low light, and it can lead to blindness if it isn't treated."
    locator "https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/VitaminA-Consumer/"
    trust authoritative

    cites "In children, vitamin D deficiency causes rickets, a disease in which the bones become soft, weak, deformed, and painful." locator "https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/VitaminD-Consumer/"
    cites "Severe thiamin deficiency leads to a disease called beriberi with the added symptoms of tingling and numbness in the feet and hands, loss of muscle, and poor reflexes." locator "https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Thiamin-Consumer/"
    cites "Getting too little folate can result in megaloblastic anemia, a blood disorder that causes weakness, fatigue, trouble concentrating, irritability, headache, heart palpitations, and shortness of breath." locator "https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Folate-Consumer/"
    cites "Vitamin B12 also helps prevent megaloblastic anemia, a blood condition that makes people tired and weak." locator "https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/VitaminB12-Consumer/"
}
